return [
    'gdpr' => [
        ['1. Introductory provisions', 'This Privacy Policy (the "Policy") describes how [Company name], with its registered office at [Registered office], Company ID: [Company ID], VAT ID: [VAT ID], registered in [Commercial register entry] ("we" or the "Controller"), collects, uses and protects the personal data you provide to us in connection with the use of our website and our services, in particular the offering of digital products and services. We are committed to protecting your privacy and process personal data in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of the Council (the "GDPR") and the applicable laws of the Czech Republic, in particular Act No. 110/2019 Coll., on the processing of personal data, as amended. If you do not agree with this Policy, please do not use our website or services.'],
        ['2. Controller of personal data', 'The controller of your personal data is: [Company name], registered office: [Registered office], Company ID: [Company ID], VAT ID: [VAT ID], e-mail: [Contact e-mail], phone: [Phone]. If you have any questions about the processing of personal data, please contact us at the e-mail address above.'],
        ['3. What personal data we collect and why', 'We collect and process personal data only for defined, legitimate purposes and only to the extent necessary to fulfil these purposes. 3.1. Data you provide: We may collect personal data that you provide to us voluntarily, for example when: Placing an order for services: first name, last name, e-mail, phone. Purpose: processing the order and providing the agreed service. Legal basis: performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). Contacting us through a form: name, e-mail, phone, content of the message. Purpose: answering your question, handling your request, preparing a price offer. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in effective communication with customers / users and pre-contractual negotiations. Subscribing to the newsletter: e-mail. Purpose: sending commercial communications and news. Legal basis: consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). 3.2. Data collected automatically: When you use our website, we may automatically collect certain information, such as: IP address. Purpose: website security, troubleshooting, traffic statistics. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Browser and device data: browser type, operating system, language. Purpose: ensuring the correct functioning of the website, optimising its display. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Website traffic data (cookies and similar technologies): pages viewed, time spent on a page, referrals from other websites. Purpose: improving the website, analysing user behaviour. Legal basis: consent (for marketing and analytics cookies, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), legitimate interest (for necessary cookies, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).'],
        ['4. How long we keep personal data', 'We keep personal data only for as long as strictly necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected, or for the period required by law. The retention period depends on the type of data and the purpose of processing: Data for the performance of a contract: for the duration of the contractual relationship and then for the period required by law for archiving accounting and tax documents (usually 10 years). Data for marketing purposes (newsletter): for the duration of your consent, but no longer than 5 years from when it was given, or until the consent is withdrawn. Data from contact forms: for the time necessary to handle your request, usually 1 year. Cookie data: the retention period depends on the type of cookie (see our Cookie Policy). After the retention period, personal data is deleted or anonymised.'],
        ['5. Who we share personal data with (recipients)', 'We share your personal data only to the extent necessary and only with verified parties, on the basis of a data processing agreement ensuring the same level of protection. These may be: IT service and hosting providers: to operate the website and information systems, for example [Hosting provider]. Marketing and analytics service providers (e.g. Google Analytics, e-mail marketing tools). Payment service providers: to process payments (e.g. banks, payment gateways). Accountants and legal advisers: to fulfil legal obligations and defend legal claims. Public authorities: where required by law (e.g. courts, police, tax office). We do not transfer personal data to countries outside the European Union or the European Economic Area without appropriate safeguards for the protection of personal data (e.g. standard contractual clauses).'],
        ['6. Your rights in connection with the processing of personal data', 'Under the GDPR you have the following rights: Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR): you have the right to obtain confirmation as to whether or not your personal data is being processed. Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR): you have the right to have inaccurate data corrected or incomplete data completed. Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR): the "right to be forgotten", where the legal grounds are met. Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR): you have the right to restrict processing in the cases set out in the GDPR. Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR): the right to receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format. Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR): the right to object to processing based on legitimate interest or for direct marketing. Right to withdraw consent (Art. 7(3) GDPR): the right to withdraw your consent at any time. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). Contact of the supervisory authority: Office for Personal Data Protection (Úřad pro ochranu osobních údajů), Pplk. Sochora 27, 170 00 Prague 7, phone: +420 234 665 800, web: www.uoou.cz'],
        ['7. Security of personal data', 'We have taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure or destruction. These measures include: data encryption (SSL/TLS), operation on secured servers with regular audits, strict access control using strong passwords, regular data backups and staff training in data security.'],
        ['8. Changes to this Policy', 'We may update this Policy from time to time. Any changes will be published on this page together with the date of the last update. We recommend checking this page regularly to stay informed about how we protect your data.'],
    ],

    'tos' => [
        ['1. Introductory provisions', 'These terms of service (the "Terms") of [Company name], with its registered office at [Registered office], Company ID: [Company ID], VAT ID: [VAT ID], registered in [Commercial register entry] (the "Seller"), govern, in accordance with Section 1751(1) of Act No. 89/2012 Coll., the Civil Code (the "Civil Code"), the mutual rights and obligations of the contracting parties arising in connection with or on the basis of a purchase contract concluded between the Seller and another natural or legal person (the "Buyer") through the Seller\'s web interface at [Website] (the "e-shop"). The provisions of the Terms form an integral part of the purchase contract. Provisions of the purchase contract that differ from the Terms take precedence over the Terms. The Seller may change or supplement the wording of the Terms. The new wording of the Terms takes effect on the day it is published on the Seller\'s website.'],
        ['2. Subject of the contract', 'The subject of the purchase contract is the sale and provision of digital products and services specified in the offer of the Seller\'s e-shop. Digital products include, but are not limited to: software, online courses, e-books, graphic templates, audio and video recordings. Services include, for example, the creation and management of online advertising.'],
        ['3. Order and conclusion of the purchase contract', 'All presentation of goods and services in the web interface of the e-shop is for information only and the Seller is not obliged to conclude a purchase contract for these goods and services. Section 1732(2) of the Civil Code does not apply. To order goods (services), the Buyer fills in the order form on the website. The order form contains in particular information about: the ordered goods (services) (the Buyer places the ordered goods in the electronic shopping cart of the web interface), the method of payment of the purchase price, the requested method of delivery, the costs associated with the delivery of the goods (services). By submitting the order, the Buyer confirms that they have read and agree to these Terms. The purchase contract is concluded when the Seller\'s acceptance of the order is delivered to the Buyer by e-mail, to the Buyer\'s e-mail address given in the order.'],
        ['4. Price and payment terms', 'Prices of goods and services include VAT unless expressly stated otherwise. Together with the purchase price, the Buyer is obliged to pay the Seller the costs associated with the delivery of the goods (services) in the agreed amount. The Seller accepts the following payment methods: bank transfer to the Seller\'s account, online card payment through a payment gateway. For cashless payment, the purchase price is due within 7 days of the conclusion of the purchase contract. The Buyer\'s obligation to pay the purchase price is fulfilled when the amount is credited to the Seller\'s account.'],
        ['5. Delivery of digital products and services', 'Digital products are delivered without undue delay after payment, usually within 24 hours, in the form of a download link, access to a members\' area, or by sending the files to the Buyer\'s e-mail. For services, delivery is agreed individually with the Buyer. Delivery costs are stated in the order and form part of the purchase price.'],
        ['6. Withdrawal from the contract', 'Due to the nature of digital content not supplied on a tangible medium, and with regard to Section 1837(l) of the Civil Code, the Buyer has no right to withdraw from the contract if the content was supplied with their prior express consent and, before the end of the withdrawal period, the Buyer declared that they had been informed that their right of withdrawal ends with the supply of the digital content. In the case of a service, a Buyer who is a consumer has the right to withdraw from the purchase contract without giving a reason within 14 days of its conclusion, provided the provision of the service has not yet begun. The notice of withdrawal must be delivered to the Seller within this period.'],
        ['7. Rights from defective performance (complaints)', 'The rights and obligations of the contracting parties regarding rights from defective performance are governed by the applicable generally binding legal regulations (in particular Sections 1914 to 1925, 2099 to 2117 and 2161 to 2174 of the Civil Code and Act No. 634/1992 Coll., on consumer protection, as amended). The Seller is liable to the Buyer that the digital product or service has no defects upon receipt. In particular, the Seller is liable to the Buyer that, at the time the Buyer received the product, it has the properties agreed by the parties, is fit for the purpose stated by the Seller and meets the requirements of the law. The Buyer exercises rights from defective performance with the Seller by e-mail at [Contact e-mail].'],
        ['8. Protection of personal data', 'The Seller undertakes to protect the Buyer\'s personal data in accordance with the applicable legal regulations, in particular the GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data). Detailed information on the processing of personal data is available in the separate Privacy Policy published on the Seller\'s website.'],
        ['9. Complaints procedure', 'On receiving a digital product or starting to use a service, the Buyer is obliged to check without undue delay that it works and corresponds to the order. If the digital product or service has defects, such as a broken download link, a discrepancy with the specification in the order or unavailable access to the members\' area, the Buyer has the right to make a complaint. The Buyer must make the complaint without undue delay after discovering the defect, by e-mail at [Contact e-mail]. The complaint must contain the identification of the Buyer (the name and e-mail used for the order), the order number, a detailed description of the defect, where applicable visual documentation of the defect, and the requested method of handling the complaint. The Seller decides on the complaint immediately, in complex cases within three working days; this period does not include the time reasonably needed for a professional assessment of the defect depending on the type of digital content or service. The complaint, including the removal of the defect, will be settled without undue delay, no later than 30 days from the date of the complaint, unless the Seller and the Buyer agree on a longer period. The Seller is liable to the Buyer that the digital product is free of defects upon delivery and has the properties agreed or that can be expected given the nature of the product. If the defect cannot be removed, the Buyer is entitled to a reasonable discount on the purchase price or to withdraw from the purchase contract in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Civil Code.'],
        ['10. Final provisions', 'If any provision of the Terms is or becomes invalid or ineffective, it is replaced by a provision whose meaning comes as close as possible to the invalid provision. These Terms are governed by the laws of the Czech Republic. All disputes arising from or in connection with these Terms will be settled by the competent courts of the Czech Republic. If a consumer dispute arises between the Seller and a consumer from a purchase contract that cannot be settled by mutual agreement, the consumer may submit a proposal for out-of-court settlement of the dispute to the designated body for out-of-court settlement of consumer disputes, which is: Czech Trade Inspection Authority (Česká obchodní inspekce), Central Inspectorate – ADR Department, Štěpánská 44, 110 00 Prague 1, web: www.coi.cz. These Terms take effect on [Effective date].'],
    ],

    'cookies' => [
        ['1. What cookies are', 'Cookies are small text files that are stored in your browser when you visit a website. They allow the website to remember information about your visit (e.g. the selected language or that you agreed to the use of cookies), which makes further browsing more convenient. Some cookies are necessary for the basic functioning of the website, others help us improve the website or show you more relevant content.'],
        ['2. Categories of cookies we use', 'We divide the cookies on our website into four categories: Necessary cookies - required for the basic functioning of the website (e.g. remembering your cookie consent); they cannot be switched off. Functional cookies - allow the website to remember your preferences (e.g. the selected language) and offer more convenient browsing. Analytics cookies - help us understand how visitors use the website (e.g. Google Analytics), so that we can improve it. Marketing cookies - used to show more relevant advertising based on your interests, also on other websites. We use analytics and marketing cookies only with your explicit consent.'],
        ['3. Specific cookies we use', 'Necessary: rpsw_cookie_consent - stores your cookie consent choice, valid for 180 days. Analytics (only with consent): _ga, _ga_* - Google Analytics, distinguishing visitors and measuring traffic, valid for up to 2 years; provider Google Ireland Limited. Marketing (only with consent): cookies of advertising and remarketing tools (e.g. Google Ads, Meta), if they are actively deployed on the website - their exact list and purpose will be added as soon as a specific tool is deployed. Functional: cookies remembering the selected language of the website.'],
        ['4. How long we keep cookies', 'The retention period depends on the type of cookie. We keep your cookie consent for 180 days; after that we ask for your consent again. Google Analytics cookies are kept according to the settings of this tool, by default for up to 2 years. Cookies remembering the language are persistent until you delete them in your browser settings or change the language again.'],
        ['5. How you can change or withdraw your consent', 'You can change or withdraw your consent to the individual categories of cookies at any time - just use the "Change cookie settings" button on this page, which reopens the banner where you can choose the individual categories. Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal. You can also delete cookies at any time in your browser settings - this also deletes the record of your consent, and the banner will be shown again on your next visit.'],
        ['6. Third-party cookies', 'For analytics purposes we use the Google Analytics service operated by Google Ireland Limited. This service may store its own cookies and process data about your behaviour on the website in accordance with Google\'s privacy policy. These cookies are stored only if you consent to analytics cookies. Details on how Google processes data can be found at policies.google.com/privacy.'],
        ['7. Contact and changes to this policy', 'If you have any questions about the use of cookies, you can contact us at [Contact e-mail]. We may update this policy from time to time, in particular in connection with changes to the tools we use on the website. The current version is always available on this page.'],
    ],
